t-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the latest deploy of v2.3.1 (error rate 18%, unhealthy in us-east, us-west, eu-west). v2.3.1 and its v2.3.1-rc were both marked unhealthy. Rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release, in all production regions. After the rollback, the service is healthy on v2.3.0 in all regions with an error rate of 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 55999, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_012DypCrzCYPKkcXpj5Fkhio", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55999, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_012DypCrzCYPKkcXpj5Fkhio", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 61124, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n- **What was wrong:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- **Version choice:** The release history isn't listed in date order. In deploy order it's v2.2.9 \u2192 v2.3.0 \u2192 v2.3.1-rc \u2192 v2.3.1. Both v2.3.1 builds are marked unhealthy, so v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is now running in all three regions. A follow-up check shows it's healthy, with the error rate down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2), which paged on-call. It describes the failure, the rollback and the result, and says the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before redeploying it. There were no open incidents beforehand, so it isn't a duplicate.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01PPFUesoyGz5ChD9z7etmLz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Bvp9Ag9656pQGnkPPrAj4Q", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The list isn't in seq order, so I sorted it by seq: v2.2.9 \u2192 v2.3.0 \u2192 v2.3.1-rc \u2192 v2.3.1. The most recent healthy release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_014joLE4DDfjhg5bR6A9uRrv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.92}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01318k21anRFCKNski8siycb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01T2uDzymkA31HV43Tanzhqv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"confidence": 0.9}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_012DypCrzCYPKkcXpj5Fkhio", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the latest deploy of v2.3.1 (error rate 18%, unhealthy in us-east, us-west, eu-west). v2.3.1 and its v2.3.1-rc were both marked unhealthy. Rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release, in all production regions. After the rollback, the service is healthy on v2.3.0 in all regions with an error rate of 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n- **What was wrong:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- **Version choice:** The release history isn't listed in date order. In deploy order it's v2.2.9 \u2192 v2.3.0 \u2192 v2.3.1-rc \u2192 v2.3.1. Both v2.3.1 builds are marked unhealthy, so v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is now running in all three regions. A follow-up check shows it's healthy, with the error rate down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2), which paged on-call. It describes the failure, the rollback and the result, and says the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before redeploying it. There were no open incidents beforehand, so it isn't a duplicate.", "type": "text"}]}]}